# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Gym Platform — Environment Variables
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your values.
# Add these same values to Vercel: Settings → Environment Variables
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Supabase (required) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Find these in your Supabase project: Settings → API
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key-here
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key-here

# ── Payments ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# There are none to configure. The profe collects payment in person
# (cash / SINPE Móvil / transfer); the app only records which plan a
# member is on. Prices are stored in `price_cents` and displayed in
# colones — see src/lib/currency.ts.

# ── Site URL (required for production) ──────────────────────────
# Used for email links, canonical URLs, and the sitemap.
# Defaults to http://localhost:3000 in development
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://yourgym.com

# ── Super Admin (recommended) ───────────────────────────────────
# Password for the /super-admin platform console.
# Must be at least 16 characters. Generate one:
#   openssl rand -base64 24
# SUPER_ADMIN_PASSWORD=your-very-strong-password-here

# ── Cron (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Secret for cron job endpoints (e.g. scheduled blog publishing)
# CRON_SECRET=your-cron-secret-here

# ── Email / SMTP ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# There is nothing to set here, and that is worth stating explicitly
# so the next person doesn't add it.
#
# The application never sends email. Every message a member receives
# (signup confirmation, password reset) is sent by Supabase Auth, so
# the SMTP credential belongs in the Supabase dashboard — not in this
# file, and not in Amplify:
#   Authentication → Emails → SMTP Settings
#   host smtp.resend.com  port 587  user resend  pass <resend api key>
# See supabase/config.toml ([auth.email.smtp]) for the full rationale.
#
# RESEND_API_KEY is consumed by ONE thing: scripts/resend-setup-dns.sh,
# which registers the sending domain and writes its SPF/DKIM records
# into Route53. Pass it on that command line for the one run that needs
# it rather than storing it here — scripts/amplify-sync-env.sh copies
# .env.local up to the hosted app, and a key no build reads has no
# business being deployed:
#   RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxx scripts/resend-setup-dns.sh
